## Outstanding Questions
Are there any other nonlinear topologies present in natural proteins or protein hybrids (such as the star or hyperbranched topology)?
Are there any other forms of mechanical bonds present in natural proteins or protein hybrids besides lassos and catenanes?
How to efficiently identify topological proteins and mechanoproteins in nature and characterize their structural features?
What is their biological significance and how does it relate to their specific topological features?
Can we design mechanical bonds and complex topologies in proteins de novo?
How can we harness the post-translational modification process for the selective biosynthesis of artificial proteins with complex topologies and/or novel mechanical bonds?
How can we achieve designed entanglement without the constraint of a rigid folded template so as to make it mobile?
How can we achieve precise, traceless, and conditionally reversible ligation to facilitate the manipulation of protein chemical topology?
How far can we push the topological complexity of proteins?
How does the topological variation change the free energy landscape of the folded proteins?
